#11146
Before A Great Iron And Stone Door~
This door is massive. It is even larger than the gates of Bazabel. It must be
solid iron and rock.  From the huge dents in it, it would seem that a few
battering rams have tried to take it down but by the decayed piles of wood to
the side, they were unsuccessful. The door is covered in numerous markings
gnomish and ghoulish. The door is heavy guarded and it seems ready to be shut
the instant it needs to be.
~
0 1 5
D1
~
~
0 0 11000
D3
Exit description~
~
0 0 11145
S
#11147
On Sorrow's Path~
The road continues south to a path which seems well tended. It leads deeper
into what appears to be a cave system.  The  air is much  cooler and the top
of the peaks are barely visible but clearly  covered in  snow. The road looks
seldom traveled and you can see no evidence  that much  trade comes through
here.  The pieces of coal, broken rope, and  rusted tools  scattered along
side the road suggest that there is some sort of  mine inside  the mountain.
~
